# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows checks files out with CRLF, while prettier defaults to
# endOfLine: "lf". The result is a formatting check that fails on a Windows laptop and
# passes on an ubuntu runner, for files nobody edited — local and CI disagreeing about
# whether the repository is clean.
#
# This is the fourth Windows-vs-Linux divergence in this project. See AGENTS.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch line endings in binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# The audit log is append-only and written by a hook on every agent write, so two branches
# almost always append different lines and conflict. `union` keeps both sides rather than
# raising a conflict — the correct semantics for a log, and the reason git ships this driver.
docs/sdlc/audit-log.md merge=union
